            concept: "Containers share the host, so limits and least privilege stop one greedy or compromised container from hurting the rest. docker run --memory 512m --cpus 1.0 caps a container's memory and CPU, and --read-only makes its filesystem read-only except for mounted volumes. Running as a non-root user (USER app in the Dockerfile) limits the damage if the application is compromised, and --cap-drop ALL removes Linux capabilities the container does not need. Never bake secrets into an image — pass them at runtime with environment variables or a secrets manager, because anyone with the image can read its layers.",
