            introduction: "In this lesson you will learn multi-stage Docker builds. A multi-stage build compiles in one image and ships only the result in a second, tiny image.",
            concept: "A multi-stage build compiles in one image and ships only the result in a second, tiny image. The first stage (FROM node:20 AS build) installs dependencies and compiles the app, then COPY --from=build /app/dist /app/dist copies just the output into a slim runtime image. The final image contains no compiler, no source, and no dev dependencies, so it is smaller and has a smaller attack surface. This pattern is the standard way to ship compiled languages like Go, Rust and TypeScript in containers.",
