            concept: "ConfigMaps and Secrets separate configuration from container images, so the same image runs in dev, staging and production. A ConfigMap holds plain configuration such as feature flags and URLs, while a Secret holds sensitive data such as passwords and tokens, stored base64-encoded (which is not encryption — treat Secrets carefully and use an external secret manager for real production). Pods consume them as environment variables or as mounted files. Changing a ConfigMap does not automatically restart Pods, so a common pattern is to roll the Deployment after a config change.",
