            introduction: "In this lesson you will learn Terraform state. The state file is Terraform's memory: it maps your configuration to the real resources it created.",
            concept: "The state file is Terraform's memory: it maps your configuration to the real resources it created. terraform.tfstate records every resource's ID and attributes, so Terraform knows what already exists and what to change. Local state works for learning but breaks teams: two people applying at once can corrupt it, and it can contain secrets in plain text. Remote state in S3 with DynamoDB locking (or Terraform Cloud) stores it centrally and locks it during applies. Never edit state by hand except through terraform state commands, and never commit state files to Git.",
