            concept: "A web server listens on a port, reads an HTTP request, and sends back a response — usually a file, or a reply from an application behind it. The browser sends a request line (GET /index.html HTTP/1.1), headers, and optionally a body; the server replies with a status code (200 OK, 404 Not Found, 500 Server Error), headers, and a body. Nginx is an event-driven server that handles tens of thousands of simultaneous connections with a small number of worker processes, which is why it powers a large share of the world's busiest sites. It can serve static files directly, proxy to an application, cache responses, and terminate TLS.",
